<!-- OPPORTUNITY PROCESS -->
<section class="section section-brown" id="process">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">The opportunity-building system</span>
      <h2>Turn Learning Into Something You Can Use</h2>
      <p>
        Learning becomes more useful when it produces a visible
        result and connects to a real-world opportunity.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="process-grid">

      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="process-number">1</div>
        <h3>Learn</h3>
        <p>Acquire the knowledge and understand the requirements.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="process-number">2</div>
        <h3>Build</h3>
        <p>Practice through projects, exercises, and real tasks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="process-number">3</div>
        <h3>Prove</h3>
        <p>Document results, demonstrate ability, and collect evidence.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="process-number">4</div>
        <h3>Connect</h3>
        <p>Find employers, customers, institutions, and relevant networks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="process-number">5</div>
        <h3>Convert</h3>
        <p>Use your preparation to pursue a job, credential, contract, or venture.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- EDUCATION -->
<section class="section section-light" id="education">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Pathway 01</span>
      <h2>Traditional Education and Financial Access</h2>
      <p>
        Formal education can provide structured learning,
        recognized qualifications, and access to institutional
        opportunities. Research the complete cost before enrolling.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-grid">

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>What to Investigate</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Program admission requirements</li>
          <li>Total tuition and mandatory fees</li>
          <li>Books, equipment, transportation, and living expenses</li>
          <li>Scholarships and grants</li>
          <li>Employer tuition assistance</li>
          <li>Credit transfer and prior learning policies</li>
          <li>Graduation and employment outcomes</li>
          <li>Professional licensing requirements</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Questions Before Applying</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Does this program qualify me for my intended opportunity?</li>
          <li>Can I study part-time or online?</li>
          <li>What funding is available?</li>
          <li>Are there lower-cost equivalent programs?</li>
          <li>Can I gain experience while studying?</li>
          <li>Will the credential be recognized by employers?</li>
          <li>What happens if I need to pause my studies?</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

    </div>

    <div class="evidence-list">
      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Financial evidence</strong>
        Document tuition, fees, aid eligibility, payment schedules,
        and the remaining amount you would need to cover.
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Academic evidence</strong>
        Compare course requirements, program outcomes,
        accreditation where applicable, and credit policies.
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Career evidence</strong>
        Identify actual job requirements and determine whether
        the program supports the roles you intend to pursue.
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- SELF EDUCATION -->
<section class="section" id="self-education">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Pathway 02</span>
      <h2>Build a Self-Education Program</h2>
      <p>
        Independent learning works best when it has a defined
        objective, a learning sequence, scheduled practice,
        and a way to verify progress.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-grid">

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Create a Learning Sequence</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Identify the career or business outcome.</li>
          <li>Research the skills required to reach it.</li>
          <li>Separate foundational skills from advanced skills.</li>
          <li>Find courses, books, and reliable instruction.</li>
          <li>Schedule practice around your available time.</li>
          <li>Build projects that apply what you learn.</li>
          <li>Review mistakes and repeat difficult tasks.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Use an Evidence Ladder</h3>

        <div class="evidence-list">
          <div class="evidence-item">
            <strong>Stage 1 — Understanding</strong>
            Explain the concept in your own words.
          </div>

          <div class="evidence-item">
            <strong>Stage 2 — Practice</strong>
            Complete guided exercises and assignments.
          </div>

          <div class="evidence-item">
            <strong>Stage 3 — Application</strong>
            Use the skill to complete an independent project.
          </div>

          <div class="evidence-item">
            <strong>Stage 4 — Demonstration</strong>
            Present the result, explain your decisions,
            and show how the work functions.
          </div>

          <div class="evidence-item">
            <strong>Stage 5 — Improvement</strong>
            Test, revise, and document what improved.
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CAREER -->
<section class="section section-light" id="career">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Pathway 03</span>
      <h2>Career Advancement and Skills Development</h2>
      <p>
        Career advancement requires more than collecting course
        completions. Connect skills to responsibilities, work
        outcomes, and the requirements of the next role.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-grid">

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Identify the Skills Gap</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Select a target job or career direction.</li>
          <li>Review several current job descriptions.</li>
          <li>Identify repeated technical and professional skills.</li>
          <li>Separate required qualifications from preferred ones.</li>
          <li>Compare those requirements with your current abilities.</li>
          <li>Prioritize the gaps that matter most.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Translate Work Into Evidence</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Document problems you helped solve.</li>
          <li>Record processes you improved.</li>
          <li>Track measurable results where available.</li>
          <li>Save examples of completed work when permitted.</li>
          <li>Collect relevant feedback and references.</li>
          <li>Connect each result to a skill or responsibility.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

    </div>

    <div class="evidence-list">
      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Example: Operational improvement</strong>
        Document the original process, the problem, your contribution,
        the change made, and the resulting improvement.
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Example: Technical development</strong>
        Build a project that demonstrates the tools, methods,
        and problem-solving abilities required by the target role.
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Example: Leadership development</strong>
        Document how you organized work, communicated expectations,
        handled a problem, or helped a team complete an objective.
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- BUSINESS -->
<section class="section" id="business">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Pathway 04</span>
      <h2>Entrepreneurship and Independent Opportunity</h2>
      <p>
        A business begins with a problem worth solving.
        Research the market, test the solution, and understand
        the financial requirements before investing heavily.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-grid">

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Validate a Business Idea</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Identify a specific customer group.</li>
          <li>Find a recurring problem they experience.</li>
          <li>Research how they currently solve it.</li>
          <li>Investigate competing products and services.</li>
          <li>Determine whether customers already pay for solutions.</li>
          <li>Test a small version of your offer.</li>
          <li>Collect feedback and evaluate actual demand.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Build the Business Foundation</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Define the product or service.</li>
          <li>Calculate startup and operating expenses.</li>
          <li>Determine pricing and delivery requirements.</li>
          <li>Research registration and legal obligations.</li>
          <li>Identify potential grants and funding programs.</li>
          <li>Create a customer acquisition strategy.</li>
          <li>Track revenue, expenses, and customer results.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

    </div>

    <div class="evidence-list">
      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Customer evidence</strong>
        Interviews, documented customer problems,
        feedback, inquiries, and actual purchases.
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Product evidence</strong>
        A working prototype, service demonstration,
        sample deliverable, or tested offer.
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <strong>Financial evidence</strong>
        Cost estimates, pricing assumptions,
        sales records, and operating projections.
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

